    "created_at": "2016-03-14T08:01:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-14T08:01:17Z",
    "body": "The spec change here that looks most appealing to me is to always reset `paused` in the media element load algorithm, just like `playbackRate` is. This would only change the behavior in instances where the `paused` attribute is false _and_ `networkState` is `HAVE_NOTHING`, which is limited to cases where `play()` is called first and then after the following microtask something causes the media element load algorithm to run. This _seems_ pretty fringe, and I could measure it in Blink.\n\n@padenot @eric-carlson @jernoble?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
