    "created_at": "2016-06-22T15:38:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-22T15:38:05Z",
    "body": "https://www.chromestatus.com/metrics/feature/timeline/popularity/1265 has been on the stable channel for a while now. Usage isn't as low as I had hoped, ~0.006%.\n\nThe risk is that if the paused state is reset, there is nothing else that causes the media resource to play, which would be pretty bad breakage. @mounirlamouri, do you have any other candidate fixes for avoiding that confusingly rejected promise? Just dropping the promise rejection bits from the media element load algorithm might do it, but it's a bit silly to leave the promise unresolved in the case where no new resource ends up selected :/\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
